# The console talks to ONE origin: the one it was served from.
#
# In production that is the `ferrogate-control-plane` Worker itself, which
# serves this console as Workers Static Assets (see
# `apps/control-plane/wrangler.toml`). Same-origin is a correctness
# requirement, not a preference: the control plane 403s any cross-site mutation
# (`sec-fetch-site`) and answers a CORS preflight only under `/admin/`, so a
# cross-origin console cannot even log in. `src/lib/config.ts` has the full
# write-up.
#
# So there is nothing to configure here for a normal run, and no variable is
# set by default.
#
# `npm run dev` serves the console at http://localhost:5173 and PROXIES
# `/admin/v1`, `/control/v1`, `/v1/admin` and `/scim/v2` to a local control
# plane (`vite.config.ts`), so the browser still sees one origin. Point that
# proxy somewhere other than the `wrangler dev` default with:
#
# VITE_CONTROL_PLANE_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# ESCAPE HATCH, not a supported production topology: send the console's API
# calls to an absolute origin instead of its own. A console configured this way
# can READ and cannot WRITE, for the reasons above. Useful only for pointing a
# locally-served console at a remote control plane while debugging.
# VITE_CONTROL_PLANE_BASE_URL=https://control-plane.example.com
